ies and Procedures may have their membership terminated. This includes failure to meet volunteer or dues obligations. Activity might include participation in various virtual gatherings, meetings, working groups, voting, and participation in discussions on online platforms or via email.\n\nIneligibility\nIf a Fellow no longer meets the qualifications for fellowship (as outlined in the eligibility criteria of the Bylaws), their affiliation will be subject to termination.\nViolations of Conduct\nFellowship or Associateship may be terminated based on the good-faith determination by the Council at the recommendation of the Affiliation Working Group that a scholar has violated the Code of Conduct or engaged in behavior materially prejudicial to RIIS 2.0’s interests.\nMEETING NOTICES\nMembership Meetings\nAll meeting notices shall be sent out by the Secretary or their designee. Notice of members’ meetings shall be sent no more than 90 days and no less than: \n30 days prior to the Annual Meeting; and\n15 days prior to a Special Meeting. Additionally, if a Special Meeting is requested by any person entitled to call such a meeting other than the Council itself, the Council shall cause notice of such meeting to be given promptly, and, in any case, within 20 days of receipt of the request.\nCouncil Meetings\nRegular meetings of the Council may be held without notice if the time and place of the meetings are fixed in advance by the Council. Special meetings of the Council may be held upon 48 hours\u0027 notice delivered personally to each Council member by electronic transmission.\nMEETINGS OF FELLOWS\nAnnual Meetings\nA general virtual meeting of the Fellows shall take place annually (the “Annual Meeting”). The specific date, time, and virtual location of the Annual Meeting will be designated by the Council. At the Annual Meeting, the announcement of the results of the election of new Councilors will be made, and Fellows will receive reports on the activities of RIIS 2.0, and determine the direction of RIIS 2.0 for the coming year.\nSpecial Meetings\nThe Council, the Chair of the Council, or a petition signed by a greater of five (5) voting Fellows or ten percent of Fellows may call a Special Meeting for any purpose at any time consistent with applicable law.\nThe Council shall cause the meeting to take place no sooner than 35 days and no later than 90 days after the request is made.\nNo business other than the business that was set forth in the Notice of the meeting may be transacted at a Special Meeting.\nAction by Written Ballot in Lieu of a Meeting\nSubject to approval by the Council, any action which may be taken at any Annual Meeting or Special Meeting may be taken without a meeting. The Council shall cause a written ballot setting forth the proposed action and any related materials to be distributed to all Fellows entitled to vote on the matter no later than 15 days prior to the deadline for submission of such Fellows’ votes.\nVoting\nExcept as otherwise provided in these Bylaws, all matters requiring a vote of the Fellows shall be decided by a simple majority of those casting electronic ballots, provided that quorum is achieved. A quorum of Fellows is achieved when at least 10% of all Fellows or 15 Fellows entitled to vote, whichever is greater, have participated in the vote. All Fellows shall be invited to vote, and those who do not submit a ballot within the prescribed two-week voting period shall be deemed to have abstained. \n"},{"ty":"as","st":"list","si":8474,"ei":8474,"sm":{"ls_ts":{"ts_un":false,"ts_un_i":true,"ts_sc":false,"ts_it_i":true,"ts_fgc2":{"hclr_color":"#000000","clr_type":0},"ts_st_i":true,"ts_bgc2":{"hclr_color":null,"clr_type":0},"ts_fs_i":true,"ts_ff_i":true,"ts_bgc2_i":true,"ts_it":false,"ts_va":"nor","ts_bd_i":true,"ts_va_i":true,"ts_fs":11.0,"ts_ff":"Arial","ts_st":false,"ts_bd":false,"ts_fgc2_i":true,"ts_sc_i":true,"ts_tw":400},"ls_id":"kix.list.1","ls_nest":1}},{"ty":"as","st":"paragraph","si":8474,"ei":