es of such decisions will be made available to Fellows within a reasonable time.\nApproving Compensation\nWhen approving compensation for employees, contractors, and any other compensation contract or arrangement, in addition to complying with the RIIS 2.0 Policies and Procedures, the Council or its designee shall also comply with the following additional requirements:\nTerms of Compensation.\nThe terms of compensation shall be approved by the Council prior to the first payment of compensation.\nFoundation of Compensation.\nThe Council shall obtain and rely upon appropriate data as defined by current US Tax Code regulations for compatibility prior to approving the terms of compensation.\nRecording of Compensation Terms.\nThe terms of compensation and the basis for approving them shall be recorded in written minutes of the meeting of the Council that approved the compensation according to the RIIS 2.0 Policies and Procedures.\n  TRANSACTIONS BETWEEN RIIS 2.0 AND COUNCILORS OR OFFICERS; DISCLOSURE OF CONFLICTS OF INTEREST\nTransactions with Councilors and Officers\nInterested Party Transactions.\nExcept as described in Section 2 of this Article, the Corporation shall not be a party to any transaction:\nin which one or more of its Councilors or Officers has a material financial interest, or \nwith any corporation, firm, association, or other entity in which one or more Councilors or Officers have a material financial interest.\nRequirements to Authorize Interested Party Transactions. \nRIIS 2.0 shall not be a party to any transaction described in Section 1 of this Article unless:\nRIIS 2.0 enters into the transaction for its own benefit; \nThe transaction is fair and reasonable to RIIS 2.0 at the time the transaction is entered into; \nprior to consummating the transaction or any part thereof, the Council authorizes or approves the transaction in good faith, by a vote of a majority of Councilors then in office (without counting the vote of the interested Councilors), and with knowledge of the material facts concerning the transaction and the interested Councilor’s or Officer’s financial interest in the transaction; \nPrior to authorizing or approving the transaction, the Council considers and, in good faith, determines after reasonable investigation that RIIS 2.0 could not obtain a more advantageous arrangement with reasonable effort under the circumstances; and \nThe minutes of the Council meeting at which such action was taken reflect that the Council considered and made the findings described in paragraphs (a) through (d) of this Section 2. \n\n    EXECUTION OF INSTRUMENTS, DEPOSITS, AND FUNDS\nExecution of Instruments\nThe Council, except as otherwise provided in these Bylaws, may by resolution authorize any Officer or agent of RIIS 2.0 to enter into any contract or execute and deliver any instrument in the name of and on behalf of RIIS 2.0, and such authority may be general or confined to specific instances. Unless so authorized, no Officer, agent, or employee shall have any power or authority to bind RIIS 2.0 by any contract or engagement to pledge its credit or to render it liable monetarily for any purpose or in any amount. \n"},{"ty":"as","st":"list","si":29970,"ei":29970,"sm":{"ls_ts":{"ts_un":false,"ts_un_i":true,"ts_sc":false,"ts_it_i":true,"ts_fgc2":{"hclr_color":"#000000","clr_type":0},"ts_st_i":true,"ts_bgc2":{"hclr_color":null,"clr_type":0},"ts_fs_i":true,"ts_ff_i":true,"ts_bgc2_i":true,"ts_it":false,"ts_va":"nor","ts_bd_i":true,"ts_va_i":true,"ts_fs":11.0,"ts_ff":"Arial","ts_st":false,"ts_bd":false,"ts_fgc2_i":true,"ts_sc_i":true,"ts_tw":400},"ls_id":"kix.list.1","ls_nest":1}},{"ty":"as","st":"paragraph","si":29970,"ei":29970,"sm":{"ps_klt_i":true,"ps_awao_i":true,"ps_sm_i":false,"ps_ls_i":true,"ps_ir_i":true,"ps_bl_i":true,"ps_sd_i":true,"ps_hdid":"h.cj5x7ovebdlg","ps_sb_i":true,"ps_ifl":36.0,"ps_sa_i":true,"ps_lslm_i":true,"ps_br_i":true,"ps_sm":1,"ps_bbtw_i":true,"ps_hd":2,"ps_kwn_i":true,"ps_bt_i":true,"ps_if